1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,052
Welcome. This is the Student Reward System: a web application for
recognising participation, recording points, and making reward
activity easier to review.

2
00:00:12,302 --> 00:00:28,094
Participation and achievement deserve to be recognised consistently.
When records and reward rules are difficult to review, it takes
extra effort to see what has been awarded. This project brings those
workflows into one place.

3
00:00:28,344 --> 00:00:45,096
An administrator signs in and uses the browser interface. Flask
handles the application routes and validation, while MySQL stores
the system records. History and leaderboard views make recorded
activity easier to review.

4
00:00:45,346 --> 00:01:01,863
Administrators can manage participant records, configure point
rules, and record awards using active activities. The system also
provides transaction history, goals, manually entered progress, and
reporting.

5
00:01:02,113 --> 00:01:19,174
Point rules define activities, values, and daily limits. In this
prepared screen, attendance is worth ten points and the active
workshop rule is worth fifty points, with a limit of one per day.
Inactive rules are also visible.

6
00:01:19,424 --> 00:01:35,141
To award points, select a participant and an active activity, then
record the transaction. The application checks awards against its
rules, including inactive activities, duplicate awards, and daily
limits.

7
00:01:35,391 --> 00:01:49,328
The leaderboard summarizes recorded points so activity can be
reviewed at a glance. This visual uses illustrative sample names and
values for privacy; check the live application for current records.

8
00:01:49,578 --> 00:02:01,700
Goals and progress are part of the system, with one important scope
note: progress is entered manually. It is not automatically
calculated from point transactions.

9
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:16,143
The project automated test run completed with twenty-nine tests
passing. These checks cover unit behavior and schema expectations.
They do not replace a live MySQL acceptance test.

10
00:02:16,393 --> 00:02:32,379
The Student Reward System provides a practical foundation for
managing participants, reward rules, point awards, and progress. Its
history and leaderboard views help make recorded activity easier to
review. Thank you.

